Duck Duck Go tutorial - 2	Test 2 description for the React.js Course	# Structured documents\n\nSometimes it's useful to have different levels of headings to structure your documents. Start lines with a `#` to create headings. Multiple `##` in a row denote smaller heading sizes.\n\n### This is a third-tier heading\n\nYou can use one `#` all the way up to `######` six for different heading sizes.\n\nIf you'd like to quote someone, use the > character before the line:\n\n> Coffee. The finest organic suspension ever devised... I beat the Borg with it.\n> - Captain Janeway	b6444c85-5b56-4301-bfe1-1474936f8483	2021-12-29 20:57:10+00	2021-12-29 20:57:10+00	60ae6236-b189-432f-86da-fd44c15d93b3	t	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1488590528505-98d2b5aba04b?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w1MTE1NTV8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxNnx8YnJvd3NlcnxlbnwwfHx8fDE2OTY0OTczOTB8MA&ixlib=rb-4.0.3&q=80&w=1080	duck-duck-go-tutorial---2-1684171020945	{"grading": false, "videoUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2fqAlgmoPo", "description": "<h1>Course Description: Duck Duck Go Tutorial - 2</h1>\\n<p>This tutorial is designed to provide participants with an in-depth understanding of the Duck Duck Go search engine, focusing on advanced features and techniques. Building upon the knowledge gained in Duck Duck Go Tutorial - 1, this course explores more advanced search strategies and advanced customization options.</p>\\n<h2>Course Details</h2>\\n<p><strong>Course Name: </strong>Duck Duck Go Tutorial - 2</p>\\n<p><strong>Duration: </strong>2 hours</p>\\n<p><strong>Prerequisites: </strong>Completion of Duck Duck Go Tutorial - 1 or equivalent knowledge</p>\\n<p><strong>Level: </strong>Intermediate</p>\\n<h2>Course Objectives</h2>\\n<p>Upon completion of this course, participants will be able to:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Utilize advanced search techniques to perform targeted searches</li>\\n<li>Employ filters and advanced operators to refine search results</li>\\n<li>Customize the Duck Duck Go search engine according to individual preferences</li>\\n<li>Understand and utilize instant answers to quickly access relevant information</li>\\n<li>Explore the privacy features and advantages of Duck Duck Go</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h2>Course Outline</h2>\\n<p>The course will cover the following topics:</p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Review of Duck Duck Go Basics</li>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Recap of Duck Duck Go search engine features</li>\\n<li>Navigating Duck Duck Go search results</li>\\n<li>Understanding the Duck Duck Go search syntax</li>\\n</ol>\\n<li>Advanced Search Techniques</li>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Using quotation marks for exact phrase searches</li>\\n<li>Excluding specific terms from search results</li>\\n<li>Using time-based searches for recent information</li>\\n</ol>\\n<li>Filters and Advanced Operators</li>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Applying filters to narrow down search results</li>\\n<li>Using advanced operators for more precise searches</li>\\n<li>Searching within specific websites or domains</li>\\n</ol>\\n<li>Customizing Duck Duck Go</li>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Changing the appearance of Duck Duck Go</li>\\n<li>Managing search settings and preferences</li>\\n<li>Adding and removing shortcuts</li>\\n</ol>\\n<li>Instant Answers</li>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Understanding and utilizing instant answers</li>\\n<li>Accessing instant answers for various types of queries (e.g., weather, calculations, definitions)</li>\\n</ol>\\n<li>Privacy Features of Duck Duck Go</li>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Exploring the privacy advantages of Duck Duck Go</li>\\n<li>Understanding Duck Duck Go's strict privacy policy</li>\\n<li>Comparing Duck Duck Go to other search engines in terms of privacy</li>\\n</ol>\\n</ol>\\n<p><em>Note: The course outline may be subject to change based on the specific needs and interests of the participants.</em></p>", "requirements": "<p>To take the Duck Duck Go tutorial course, you will need the following: 1. A computer or laptop with a stable internet connection 2. A web browser (e.g., Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari) 3. Basic knowledge of how to navigate and use a web browser 4. Ability to understand and follow instructions in English 5. Familiarity with search engines and their basic functions Please ensure that you have met these requirements before proceeding with the course.</p>", "lessonDownload": false, "lessonTabsOrder": [{"id": 1, "name": "Note"}, {"id": 2, "name": "Slide"}, {"id": 3, "name": "Video"}]}	0	NGN	\N	t	f	professional	ACTIVE
