14	2023-07-04 15:00:32.766627+00	Did people really go to space or it's all a lie?	<p>Yes, people do go to space. Human space travel haaaasss been a reality for several decades. The first human to travel into space was Yuri Gagarin, a Sooviet cosmonaut, who orbited the Earth aboard the Vostok 1 spacecraft on April 12, 1961. Since then, numerous astronauts and cosmonauts from various countries have ventured into space.</p><p>\n</p><p>Space travel is primarily conducted by space agencies such as NASA (United States), Roscosmos (Russia), ESA (European Space Agency), and others. These agencies have developed spacecraft and launch systems capable of carrying humans into space. The most notable program for human space exploration is the International Space Station (ISS), a multinational collaborative project involving multiple countries, where astronauts live and conduct scientific research in microgravity.</p><p>\n</p><p>In recent years, private space companies have also emerged, such as SpaceX, Blue Origin, and Virgin Galactic. These companies are working on developing commercial spaceflight capabilities and have already sent both crewed and uncrewed missions to space. SpaceX's Crew Dragon spacecraft, for example, has transported astronauts to and from the International Space Station.</p><p>\n</p><p>While space travel is still relatively rare and limited to a select group of highly trained individuals, ongoing advancements in technology and the efforts of both government and private organizations are making space more accessible and increasing opportunities for more people to travel to space in the future.</p><p>\n</p><p>But then again, it could all be a lie.</p><p>\n</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\n</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\n</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\n</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\n</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\n</p><p>&nbsp;</p>	30	0	89a7b4d2-fe01-4329-912a-986d6f6e1fde	didpeoplereallygotospaceoritsallalie-1688482833580
