da9f6e0f-e4b6-429f-ba8f-5c2e4748737d	2023-10-10 07:05:15.636753+00	31	<p>This question was answered in the thread&nbsp;<a href="https://webapps.stackexchange.com/a/172321/">Which formats does Telegram internal video player support?</a>&nbsp;of webapps.stackexchange</p>\n<p>Recommendations on ffmpeg commands to optimize a video to run in the Telegram player.</p>\n<p><strong>Essential</strong><br>Video codec:&nbsp;<a href="https://trac.ffmpeg.org/wiki/Encode/H.264" rel="nofollow noreferrer">x264 (avc)</a>&nbsp;or x265 (hevc)<br>audio codec: aac<br>audio channels: up to 2</p>\n<p><strong>Recommended</strong><br><code>max_muxing_queue_size 9999</code>&nbsp;- prevents memory allocation error during encoding for high-resolution videos. (Too many packets buffered for output stream)</p>\n<p><code>c:v libx264</code>&nbsp;- x264 codec, requires less CPU, avoiding crashes on old smartphones</p>\n<p><code>maxrate 4.5M</code>&nbsp;- Establishes maximum peak bitrate in complex scenes, to avoid crashes on a modest internet connection.</p>\n<p><code>crf 23</code>&nbsp;- Establishes a constant quality factor. Can be overridden by bitrate setting</p>\n<p><code>preset faster</code>&nbsp;- image optimization filter presets in the encode, which impacts the final size in a negative correlation with processing time. "Faster" delivers the best cost-benefit tradeoff according to the&nbsp;<a href="https://streaminglearningcenter.com/articles/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">trainer and author Jan Ozer</a></p>\n<p><code>flags +global_header</code>&nbsp;- Adds global metadata to the file, useful to the player</p>\n<p><code>pix_fmt yuv420p</code>&nbsp;- Greater compatibility with older smartphones</p>\n<p><code>profile:v baseline</code>&nbsp;- Greater compatibility with older smartphones</p>\n<p><code>movflags +faststart</code>&nbsp;- Rearranges the output file so that essential metadata is placed at the beginning of the file</p>\n<p><code>c:a aac</code>&nbsp;- Audio codec required by Telegram</p>\n<p><code>ac 2</code>&nbsp;- Limits up to 2 audio channels (stereo). Above that, Telegram does not execute the file.</p>\n<p><strong>Final command example:</strong></p>\n<pre class="lang-bash s-code-block"><code class="hljs language-bash">ffmpeg -i <span class="hljs-string">"input.mkv"</span> -max_muxing_queue_size 9999 -c:v libx264 -crf 23 -maxrate 4.5M -preset faster -flags +global_header -pix_fmt yuv420p -profile:v baseline -movflags +faststart -c:a aac -ac 2 <span class="hljs-string">"output.mp4"</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>For batch video optimization<br><a href="https://pypi.org/project/vidqa/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">VIDQA</a> - Python library that performs batch video optimizations, compatible with Telegram</p>	87	0
fcfeeb55-b4ae-4d91-aaa8-a72f46c29667	2023-10-10 07:05:53.739937+00	32	<p>There is a concept of Userbot among telegram users which is basically using a MTProto library to use your own account like a bot .</p>\n<p>You can check&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/RaphielGang/Telegram-Paperplane" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Telegram-Paperplane</a>&nbsp;which uses&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/LonamiWebs/Telethon" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Telethon</a>&nbsp;MTProto Library , (Referred this as just an Idea for what you want to do , Check the PMPERMIT feature which might be little bit similar to your goal) ..</p>\n<p>Unfortunately it is not written in C# , You need to find MTProto library for C# make something like this to achieve your target .</p>	87	0
27a297ec-7859-49c8-a62c-e1cc7a44b43d	2023-10-10 07:06:04.28886+00	32	<p>You cannot access your account with the telegram bot api in that way, so you will have to use&nbsp;<a href="https://core.telegram.org/tdlib" rel="nofollow noreferrer">the Telegram API</a></p>\n<p>greetings,</p>\n<p>Mike</p>	87	0
89f6400e-20db-4aa6-a5cc-74d7f24f1dca	2023-10-10 07:06:55.770826+00	33	<p>Currently, Telegram Bot API does not provide such parameter. That being, you need to wait for the server's response and check if it went OK before sending the next message.</p>\n<p>If you use NodeJs, there's a module called&nbsp;<a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/tgfancy" rel="nofollow noreferrer">tgfancy</a>&nbsp;that handles&nbsp;<a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/tgfancy#ordered-sending" rel="nofollow noreferrer">ordered message sending</a>&nbsp;(along with polling and so many other things) for you.</p>\n<p>Thibauld's answer adds a really nice suggestion of using the&nbsp;<a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#sendchataction" rel="nofollow noreferrer">sendChatAction</a>&nbsp;method in order to make the interaction look more conversational. My only point is that a bot is not supposed to pretend it is a human, so there's no need to make it look like there's one typing. That being,&nbsp;<code>sendChatAction</code> would serve to the purpose of indicating that your bot has received the user's message and is processing it.</p>	87	0
b948a61d-7fc7-4fa1-ae85-0343dbcfc63a	2023-10-10 07:06:43.188854+00	33	<p>Telegram bots are supposed to have a human-like interaction. So my advise to avoid your problem would be to define a sort&nbsp;<code>TYPINGSPEED</code>&nbsp;constant and combine it with the&nbsp;<code>sendChatAction()</code>&nbsp;bot api call so that if "feels" like your messages are actually being written by a 'fast-typing' human being.</p>\n<p>In ruby, it would give something like this :</p>\n<pre><code>your_msg.split("\\n").each do |line|\n    writing_time=line.length/TYPINGSPEED\n    TelegramBot.client.api.sendChatAction(chat_id: chat_id, action: "typing")\n    sleep(writing_time)\n    TelegramBot.client.api.sendMessage(your_options)\nend\n</code></pre>\n<p><a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#sendchataction" rel="nofollow">sendChatAction</a>&nbsp;nicely displays "nameofyourbot is writing..." on the user screen.</p>\n<p>Of course, the drawback with this code is that the process handling the answer won't return before several seconds if your message is long (because of the use of the&nbsp;<code>sleep</code>&nbsp;function). So depending of the number of simultaneous users using your bot, you'd better do some capacity planning and spawn as many process as you need to make sure your bot can handle the number of parallel discussions required.</p>\n<p>I am doing this myself and I never experienced the issue you are describing.</p>	87	1
daf792a4-8897-4338-9d41-7956a819d75c	2023-10-10 07:07:53.788275+00	34	<p>They say you have to use the answerCallbackQuery method</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>"URL that will be opened by the user's client. If you have created a Game and accepted the conditions via @Botfather, specify the URL that opens your game &ndash; note that this will only work if the query comes from a callback_game button.</p>\n<p>Otherwise, you may use links like telegram.me/your_bot?start=XXXX that open your bot with a parameter."</p>\n</blockquote>	87	0
41afa9a9-521a-49a7-8d1e-f3de844be08c	2023-10-10 07:08:45.655394+00	34	<p>i solve in this way:</p>\n<pre><code>if(isset($update["callback_query"])) {\n  $parameters["method"] = "answerCallbackQuery";\n  $parameters["callback_query_id"] = $update["callback_query"]["id"];\n  $parameters["url"] = "&lt;url_game&gt;";\n  echo json_encode($parameters);\n}\n\n$parameters = array('chat_id' =&gt; $chatId);\n// method &egrave; il metodo per l'invio di un messaggio (cfr. API di Telegram)\n$parameters["method"] = "sendGame";\n$parameters["game_short_name"] = "prova";\n</code></pre>\n<p>Explanation: In the first part is sent to the photo set from botfather. When you decide to play a callback_query you are created. We must send then the url of our html5 code</p>	87	0
9497290d-886c-41d3-bf6d-49dc0ae5f6a2	2023-10-10 07:09:28.613846+00	35	<p>Please take a look to the ForceReply&nbsp;<a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#forcereply" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#forcereply</a>: when you send a message using&nbsp;<code>sendMessage</code> (e.g. on inline button click), you can use it to automatically open reply dialog for that message. Given this.</p>	87	0
