# Web Development Course - Zero to Hero\n\n## Lesson: HTML (Part 2)\n\n### Lesson Objective\n- Understand advanced HTML concepts.\n- Learn how to structure content with HTML5 semantic elements.\n- Apply CSS styles to HTML elements for enhanced visual presentation.\n\n### Lesson Outline\n1. HTML Recap\n   - Brief review of HTML basics covered in Part 1.\n   - Discuss the importance of proper HTML document structure.\n   - Revisit HTML tags, attributes, and their usage.\n\n2. HTML5 Semantic Elements\n   - Introduction to HTML5 semantic elements and their purpose.\n   - Explain the benefits of using semantic elements for both developers and search engines.\n   - Provide examples and show how to use semantic elements such as `header`, `nav`, `section`, `article`, `aside`, `footer`, etc.\n\n3. Structuring Content with Semantic Elements\n   - Explain the importance of proper content organization in a web page.\n   - Demonstrate how to structure a web page using semantic elements.\n   - Show how to group related content using elements like `section` and `article`.\n   - Discuss the appropriate use of headings (`h1` to `h6`) and how they contribute to accessibility and SEO.\n\n4. CSS Styling for HTML Elements\n   - Introduction to CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) and its role in web page presentation.\n   - Overview of CSS syntax and basic selectors.\n   - Demonstrate how to apply CSS styles to HTML elements.\n   - Cover various ways of styling elements, including inline styles, internal stylesheets, and external stylesheets.\n\n5. Hands-on Practice\n   - Provide a practice exercise for students to reinforce their understanding of the covered topics.\n   - Students will be given a web page with unstructured content and asked to apply appropriate semantic elements and CSS styles.\n\n6. Summary and Next Steps\n   - Recap the key concepts learned during the lesson.\n   - Discuss the importance of practicing and further exploring HTML and CSS.\n   - Share additional resources and recommended exercises for further self-study.\n\n**Note:** It is recommended that students complete "HTML (Part 1)" before taking this lesson to ensure a strong foundation in HTML basics.	\N	\N	d24d9991-1bcd-4020-8f1c-3cdc2d42a28a	10d9786b-cdac-4915-b5cd-d988defd332b	2021-10-16 23:20:40.359599+00	2023-08-04 17:04:09.028234+00	HTML (Part 2)	f	2021-10-31 00:00:00+00	14f8615e-e17e-47a2-b30a-8931ce705f42	t		\N	t	[]
