# ACCOUNTING & RECORD KEEPING\nRecords are essential tools for successful management of the flock\n## Purpose of Records\n1.Measure profits and access the financial ability of the business\n2. Provide data  for business /operation analysis\n3. Assist in obtaining loans\n4. Measure profitability of individual operation\n5. Assist in analysis of new investments\n6. Production of balance sheet\n7. Compare performance of batches\n8. Compare performance of selection\n9.Reference to previous success\n10.Avoid previous mistakes\n11. Copy standard procedures \n## Different record keeping Forms Used in Poultry Production\n### Mortality death of birds \nEvery day record any bird that does not survive\n### Feed used\nDaily records of the quantity of feeds fed to birds\n### Vaccinations	\N	\N	0557ce08-93a5-4340-8dfc-0dca7d09086e	ef80a663-0ece-41e2-bd45-8e2ada1e8f22	2022-10-25 08:33:50.799281+00	2022-10-29 05:09:14.32266+00	Accounting & Record Keeping	f	2022-10-27 00:00:00+00	e100784f-d1cf-4719-b74c-0b6498d8c4cd	f		\N	t	[]
<p>Sure!</p>\n<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," width="1013" height="691"></p>\n<p>Here are a few interactive lesson activities for the lesson on "Analytics and Measurement":</p>\n<p><strong>Activity 1</strong>: Analyzing User Data Create a form where students can input user data such as age, location, and interests. Use JavaScript to collect and store this data in variables. Then, display the collected data on the webpage using HTML elements and CSS styling. This activity will help students understand how to collect and analyze user data for better decision making in analytics.</p>\n<p id="collectedData"></p>\n<p><strong>Activity 2</strong>: Setting up Google Analytics Guide students through the process of setting up Google Analytics for a website. Explain the steps involved, such as creating a Google Analytics account, generating the tracking code, and adding it to the website. Provide a sample website where students can practice implementing Google Analytics. This activity will help students understand how to measure website traffic and user behavior using analytics tools.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Go to <a href="https://analytics.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://analytics.google.com</a> to create a Google Analytics account.</p>\n<p>Follow these steps to set up Google Analytics for your website:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Create a new property in Google Analytics</li>\n<li>Generate the tracking code</li>\n<li>Add the tracking code to your website</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Once you have set up Google Analytics, use the following sample website to practice implementing it:</p>\n<p><code>\n&lt;!-- Add this code to the &lt;head&gt; section of your HTML --&gt;<br>\n&lt;script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=UA-XXXXXXXXX-X"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;<br>\n&lt;script&gt;<br>\n  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];<br>\n  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}<br>\n  gtag('js', new Date());<br>\n  gtag('config', 'UA-XXXXXXXXX-X');<br>&nbsp;&lt;/script&gt;</code></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Activity 3</strong>: Interpreting Data Visualization Provide students with a data visualization chart, such as a bar graph or pie chart, and ask them to analyze and interpret the data. Encourage students to identify trends, make comparisons, and draw conclusions based on the provided data. This activity will enhance students' ability to analyze and derive insights from visualized data.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Based on the data visualization chart above, answer the following questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Which category has the highest value?</li>\n<li>Which category has the lowest value?</li>\n<li>Are there any significant differences between the categories?</li>\n<li>What conclusions can you draw from the data?</li>\n</ol>\n<p>These activities will engage students in hands-on learning and encourage them to apply the concepts of analytics and measurement in a practical manner. Remember to adapt the code snippets and instructions as per your specific teaching requirements and preferences.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If you've got any questions please let me know.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," width="383" height="265"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>	\N	https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vRTLSaaUDgG4xbOY8yPZZVRSrYsyWvZQMl37gmMtmiJl0O_fJ4Y6wuED7JuQ1Yr2W-soCbnrkqWgA25/embed	f8ee2577-44be-482f-ab5b-061717fdb3f9	5b8126c6-cf04-4dfd-8679-cb24e77f888f	2023-08-27 03:36:25.708283+00	2023-09-26 10:27:04.20678+00	Analytics and Measurement	f	2023-08-27 03:36:20.528+00	0729a995-ce20-468d-aac3-f8d9ea927989	f		9	f	[{"link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b3szQPSRfjY&t=29s&ab_channel=MITOpenCourseWare", "type": "youtube", "metadata": {}}]
# Here is my situation:\n\nI have been working in a staffing company (lets call it company ABC, its a fortune 500 company) since May 2014 and in march 2016 they have deployed me in one of their client's offices (lets call it XYZ, one of the leading manufacturers of wind turbines). I am working in the HR department and the roles and responsibilities i have been given in XYZ is more of a direct match to what is mentioned in my applicable NOC when compared to ABC.\n\nThe thing is, ABC and XYZ have a global agreement that all employees in the HR department of XYZ except for the top management will be on the payroll of ABC. I have got 2 reference letters on the letterhead of my parent company ABC:\n\n1) letter signed by my manager when i was working in ABC\n2) letter signed by my manager in XYZ (and she is on the payroll of ABC as well)\n\nso if CIC calls my manager when i was working in ABC, that shouldnt be an issue. I have submitted a deputation letter from ABC saying that i have been moved to XYZ from march 2016. I have however not submitted any letter from a direct employee of XYZ as mentioned previously, they are the top management and might not be aware of my day to day duties. I have mentioned the direct desk number and mobile phone number of my manager in XYZ in the body of the letter but the letterhead contains the number of ABC. Assuming, CIC calls my manager on her mobile phone and desk number and she doesnt pick up and then they call the number in the letter head which is the number of ABC and finds out that she is not working there but is in another office, will there be any issue?\n\ni know it kind of sounds complicated and I myself got confused a bit explaining all this :) any answer would be helpful !	https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g-zP9lt004E&ab_channel=UchihaVillage	\N	d7f39be1-63a5-43bf-b3aa-6b64ffe8c12e	a44ff6dc-3700-42ea-859c-b1d24caf07bb	2021-12-29 19:00:02.972021+00	2021-12-29 19:00:02.972021+00	Lesson 1	f	2021-12-29 19:00:01.546+00	\N	t		\N	t	[]
