<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<body>\n  <h1>Lesson Note: Red-Shift</h1>\n\n  <h2>Introduction</h2>\n  <p>\n    In this lesson, we will be discussing the concept of red-shift and its significance in understanding the universe. Red-shift refers to the phenomenon where light from a celestial object appears to be shifted towards the red end of the electromagnetic spectrum. It is an essential concept in studying the vastness and evolution of our universe.\n  </p>\n\n  <h2>The Doppler Effect</h2>\n  <p>\n    To understand red-shift, it is important to grasp the basic concept known as the Doppler Effect. The Doppler Effect is the change in frequency or wavelength of a wave in relation to an observer who is moving relative to the wave source. This effect is observed not only in sound waves but also in electromagnetic waves, such as light.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Red-shift and Blue-shift</h3>\n  <p>\n    Red-shift occurs when an object, such as a galaxy or star, moves away from an observer. As a result, the wavelengths of light emitted by the object become stretched, causing a shift towards longer wavelengths, i.e., the red end of the spectrum. This indicates that the object is moving away from us, and the greater the red-shift, the faster the object is receding.\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    Conversely, blue-shift occurs when an object moves towards the observer, causing the wavelengths of light to compress, resulting in a shift towards shorter wavelengths, i.e., the blue end of the spectrum. This indicates that the object is moving closer to us.\n  </p>\n\n  <h2>Applications in Cosmology</h2>\n  <p>\n    Red-shift has profound implications for understanding the structure and expansion of the universe. It provides evidence for the Big Bang theory, which suggests that the universe originated from a single point and has been expanding ever since. The red-shift observed in the light from distant galaxies indicates that they are moving away from us in all directions, supporting the notion of an expanding universe.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Hubble's Law</h3>\n  <p>\n    Red-shift measurements have enabled scientists, such as Edwin Hubble, to establish a relationship between the distance of a galaxy and its red-shift. This relationship, now known as Hubble's Law, states that the speed at which a galaxy is moving away from us is directly proportional to its distance. Hubble's Law played a crucial role in calculating the age of the universe and providing evidence for the Big Bang theory.\n  </p>\n\n  <h2>Conclusion</h2>\n  <p>\n    Red-shift is a fundamental concept in astrophysics that has revolutionized our understanding of the universe. By studying the red-shift of light from distant objects, scientists can deduce valuable information about the origin, expansion, and structure of our vast cosmos. This concept continues to shape our exploration and knowledge of our solar system and beyond.\n  </p>\n</body>\n</html>	https://www.youtube.com/embed/-mQ41yA6LaA		c2340c25-a5c2-42e9-bc1a-4cbdc0c4d4b3	02f4fea7-142e-45be-801c-420c7f9c2a5e	2023-07-04 11:25:17.543409+00	2023-08-24 16:43:38.573191+00	Red-Shift	f	2023-07-04 11:25:07.645+00	a062a70c-6975-43de-83d6-669489cedfa2	f		3	t	[]
