<!-- Lesson Note -->\n<p>Welcome to the first lesson of the HTML for Absolute Beginners course! In this lesson, we will cover the basics of HTML and get an overview of web development.</p>\n<h3>What is HTML?</h3>\n<p>HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. It is the standard markup language used for creating web pages and web applications. HTML provides the structure and content of a webpage by using a set of predefined tags.</p>\n<p>HTML documents are made up of a hierarchy of elements. Each element is represented by a start tag and an end tag, and can contain other elements or text content.</p>\n<h3>Why Learn HTML?</h3>\n<p>HTML is the foundation of web development. It is essential for anyone who wants to create web pages, design websites, or become a web developer. By learning HTML, you will have the skills to create and structure content on the web.</p>\n<p>HTML is also a great starting point for learning other web technologies, such as CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) and JavaScript. It provides the necessary structure for applying styles to web pages and adding interactivity.</p>\n<h3>Basics of Web Development</h3>\n<p>Web development involves creating and maintaining websites. It includes both the front-end development, which focuses on the user interface and user experience, and the back-end development, which handles server-side logic and data management.</p>\n<p>Front-end development deals with everything the user sees and interacts with on a website. It includes HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, which together create the visual design, layout, and interactivity of web pages.</p>\n<p>Back-end development involves working with server-side languages like PHP, Python, or Ruby, and databases to handle data processing, storage, and retrieval. It also includes server configuration and management.</p>\n<h3>Getting Started with HTML</h3>\n<p>To get started with HTML, you only need a text editor and a web browser. You can write HTML code in any plain text editor, such as Notepad or Sublime Text. Then, save the file with a .html extension. To view the HTML page, simply open it in a web browser.</p>\n<p>HTML code is written using tags, which are enclosed in angle brackets (&lt; &gt;). Tags define the structure and elements of a webpage. Some common tags used in HTML include , ,</p>	\N	\N	194a3c8a-bc27-4c8a-8c60-444481ba9640	935e7ec1-073d-4975-b495-3fdfd3bb90f7	2023-10-15 11:58:59.813101+00	2023-11-07 10:15:28.077225+00	Introduction to HTML and Web Development	f	2023-10-15 11:58:48.769+00	0729a995-ce20-468d-aac3-f8d9ea927989	f	\N	\N	f	[]
