<h2>Learning Objectives:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Understand the basics of SQL</li>\n<li>Learn how to write simple SQL queries</li>\n<li>Gain familiarity with the Supabase backend development platform</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Lesson Content:</h2>\n<p>Welcome to the first lesson of the course "SQL For Beginners: Learn Backend Development with Supabase". In this lesson, we will provide an introduction to SQL and cover the basics of writing SQL queries.</p>\n<h3>What is SQL?</h3>\n<p>SQL stands for Structured Query Language. It is a programming language used to manage and manipulate relational databases. SQL allows users to store, retrieve, and modify data in a structured manner.</p>\n<h3>Why Learn SQL?</h3>\n<p>SQL is widely used in the IT and software development industry. It is the standard language for managing relational databases, making it essential for anyone aspiring to become a backend developer. SQL skills are highly sought after by employers, and mastering the language will open up a wide range of career opportunities.</p>\n<h3>Basic SQL Queries:</h3>\n<p>In this lesson, we will focus on the following types of SQL queries:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>SELECT:</strong> Used to retrieve data from a database</li>\n<li><strong>INSERT:</strong> Used to insert new data into a database</li>\n<li><strong>UPDATE:</strong> Used to update existing data in a database</li>\n<li><strong>DELETE:</strong> Used to delete data from a database</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Supabase: The Backend Development Platform</h3>\n<p>Throughout this course, we will be using Supabase as our backend development platform. Supabase is an open-source alternative to Firebase and provides a set of tools and services for building applications with SQL.</p>\n<h2>Summary:</h2>\n<p>By the end of this lesson, you should have a basic understanding of SQL and its importance in backend development. You should also be familiar with the Supabase platform and its key features.</p>	\N	\N	a25904dd-cee0-442f-ac3a-a1103fc8e4c8	abfd6fb8-6231-4da7-8967-7aceb035cd14	2023-10-11 11:55:20.456099+00	2023-11-10 22:58:57.26294+00	Introduction to SQL: Understanding the Basics	f	2023-12-04 00:00:00+00	0729a995-ce20-468d-aac3-f8d9ea927989	f		\N	f	[]
