528	{}	261	Overlapping scenarios in BIM fields includes Technology, process and policy TPP\nBIM Technology Field: the technology field clusters a group of players who specializes in developing software, hardware, equipment and networking system necessary to increase efficiency, productivity and profitability of AECO sectors. This includes organization which generate software solutions and equipment of direct and indirect applicability to the design, construction and operation of facilities eg. Autodesk, ALLPLAN\n\nThe Policy Field: this clusters a group of players focused on preparing practitioners, delivering research, distributing benefits, allocating risks and minimsing conflicts within the AECO industry. These players do not generate any construction products but are specialized organization like insurance companies, research center, educational institutions and regulatory and contractual roles in the design, construction and operation process e.g COREN, ARCON, QSRBN , FUTA, UI, OAU, Bells Tech, Julius Berger etc\n\nThe process Field: clusters a group of players who procure, design, construct, manufacture, use, manage and maintain structures. These include facility owners, architects, Engineers, contractors, facility managers and all other AECO industry player involved in the ownership and operations of building or structures NSE, NIA, Infraworks	ec71424b-8184-427a-ad2a-3be756e14984	59847aff-e1b0-490f-96d0-f340ca792d54	2
